{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter and Sally Plan a Road Trip", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Boston's Nicknames", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 15, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people and places in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of people and places in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of people and places in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of people and places in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of people and places in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of people and places in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.   Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Past Tense and Past Continuous tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished.</br> You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that was happening at a time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.</br> Regular verbs end in <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"italic\">-ied</span>.</br> Irregular verbs change in different ways.</br> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">did</span> followed by the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask \u2026 ?</span> </br><span class=\"italic\">Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"italic\">to do</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For Past Continuous, we add <span class = \"italic\">was/were + verb -ing</span> to verbs.</br> Some verbs need a change to the last letter to add <span class = \"italic\">-ing</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"turn\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"turned\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were turning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"build\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"built\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were building\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"think\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were thinking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"approach\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"approached\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were approaching\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"win\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"won\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were winning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"expand\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"expanded\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were expanding\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I was always watching sports games on TV when my parents called me to do homework.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Many attractions were built downtown.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Sally was thinking about the name, a City Upon a Hill, when she approached a new hill.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to approach", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move closer", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As Sally approached the hill on her bike, she knew it would be tough riding up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about a city and its culture.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "latte", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a specialty coffee made with \u00bc espresso and \u00be steamed milk", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally loves her latte every morning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "champion", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the winner of the final game of the sports season", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Boston Red Sox were Major League Baseball champions in 2014.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hockey", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a team sport played on ice with 6 players on each side using a small black round object called a puck, and a stick", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Boston Bruins is the city's champion hockey team.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "yard", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the grass space surrounding the home often planted with trees and flowers", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Families love to keep their yards beautiful to sit and play in.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to expand", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to increase in size and population ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Boston expanded a lot over the years.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "local", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who is from a particular city ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The locals of Boston are really proud of their culture and sports teams.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob07